{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `n`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `n` is a top-level data variable and is observed exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement, `n ~ binomial_logit(...)`. Other data variables (`I`, `N`, `x1`, `x2`) are context inputs used as sizes, predictors, or constants and are not protected. Each parameter has exactly one built-in prior before it is used in the model block.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> I;
  array[I] int<lower=0> n;
  array[I] int<lower=0> N;
  vector[I] x1; // seed type
  vector[I] x2; // root extract
}
transformed data {
  vector[I] x1x2;
  x1x2 = x1 .* x2;
}
parameters {
  real alpha0;
  real alpha1;
  real alpha12;
  real alpha2;
  vector[I] c;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[I] b;
  b = c - mean(c);
}
model {
  alpha0 ~ normal(0.0, 1.0); // Narrower priors
  alpha1 ~ normal(0.0, 1.0);
  alpha2 ~ normal(0.0, 1.0);
  alpha12 ~ normal(0.0, 1.0);
  sigma ~ cauchy(0, 1);

  c ~ normal(0.0, sigma);
  n ~ binomial_logit(N,
                     alpha0 + alpha1 * x1 + alpha2 * x2 + alpha12 * x1x2 + b);
}
